    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to New Mexico?",
      "a": "New Mexico has $1.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. New Mexico recorded obligations of $11.7B in FY22, $12.4B in FY23, $13.1B in FY24, $13.5B in FY25, and $15.8B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations and FY2027 totals are partial."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in New Mexico?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy obligated $1.5B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $17.3M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $15M, and other agencies with obligations in FY2027 to date include the Department of Homeland Security with $11.2M and the Department of Justice with $5.5M."
